## Exposure and independence

The same model/effort and previous source-exposed reviewer/package-author history are material limits. Parent knew the candidate mechanism before the neutral task and read the candidate draft before comparison. The candidate author also authored the selection memo, single-port body and corrected joint source. There was no direct proof coordination with that author. The new stochastic-domination/count/covariance argument was read only after the independent proof was sealed; the comparison is therefore source-exposed, while the sealed independent TV/allocation/quantum argument predates candidate exposure.

The selection memo itself remains substantively unread. Its bytes and nested freeze were hashed after the independent seal solely because they are members of the candidate's source/recovery package. No result from that memo is a theorem premise here. No old scientific diagnostic, external-paper extraction or author scientific program was replayed.

There were zero new scientific executions. Exact algebra and analytic counterexamples sufficed. Only copying, source hashing, exact text-diff reconstruction, syntax parsing and metadata receipt validation ran. Their actual output is preserved under `metadata_runs`; no PASS count is presented as mathematical independence. No model override, delegation, W/Git/PR/audit/axiom/prompt/checkpoint/lock change occurred.
